# steps/merge-callable-r48.md S1: a held callable's call is a call (l2_node_has_call) -- on the right of && it runs
# only when the left holds.  The root calls go(0) before add5's statement runs, so add5 holds no node yet: a call of
# it there would stop the program in its held helper.  go(0) must not make it, so the entry is 7.
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    return: addN
int: r 0
r: go(0)
add5: makeAdder 5
fn: go (int: t) int
    int: ok 7
    if: t = 1 && (add5: 1) = 6
        ok: 81
    return: ok
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
